+# vshell: dwrite belongs to this unconditional list, not only inside the
+# ENABLE_VIDEO block further down.
+#
+# The Skia font backend (platform/graphics/win/FontCacheSkiaWin.cpp) calls
+# DWriteCreateFactory() unconditionally, but upstream only links dwrite through
+# the MediaFoundation INTERFACE library, which does not exist when
+# ENABLE_VIDEO=OFF. That turns video-off into a LINK failure (the whole of WebCore
+# compiles fine, which makes it look unrelated):
+#   lld-link: error: undefined symbol: __declspec(dllimport) DWriteCreateFactory
+#   >>> referenced by platform\graphics\win\FontCacheSkiaWin.cpp:54
+# Linking an import library twice is harmless, so this is safe when video is on.
 list(APPEND WebCore_LIBRARIES
     crypt32
+    dwrite
     iphlpapi
     usp10
     ws2_32
